==English==
[[File:Loganberries on the plant.jpg|thumb|'''loganberries''' on the plant]]
{{wikipedia}}
{{wikispecies|Rubus loganobaccus}}

===Etymology===
{{compound|en|Logan|berry}}, named for the American lawyer and [[horticulturist]] {{w|James Harvey Logan}} (1841-1928).

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[hybrid]] [[berry]], produced by [[crossing]] a [[raspberry]] with a [[blackberry]], considered a species {{taxlink|Rubus loganobaccus|species}}, a [[variety]] {{taxlink|Rubus ursinus var. loganobaccus|variety}}, or a [[nothospecies]] {{taxlink|Rubus × loganobaccus|nothospecies}}.
#* {{RQ:Hollinghurst Line|page=379|passage=Brad hesitated, peering at the grid of spun sugar that jutted from his '''loganberry''' parfait.}}

